<!-- SYNTHETIC FIXTURE: fully fictional data (Muster GmbH / DE000000000).
     NEGATIVE TWIN of synth-ubl-good-fullshape_ubl.xml (T-VHR.19). Byte-for-byte
     identical to the good full-shape XRechnung 3.0 UBL invoice EXCEPT ONE
     targeted, economically-meaningful defect: the document-level GRAND TOTAL is
     overstated. Both BT-112 (TaxInclusiveAmount) and BT-115 (PayableAmount) —
     the two mutually-required-equal fields that jointly represent the grand
     total — are set to 990.60 instead of the reconciling 900.60. Every other
     value, and every mandatory BG group, is unchanged from the good twin:
       * BG-4 SELLER + BG-6 seller contact + BT-31 VAT id,
       * BG-7 BUYER + BT-10 BuyerReference,
       * BG-13 delivery with BT-72 Actual delivery date (Leistungsdatum),
       * 4x BG-25 invoice lines across TWO VAT rates (19% and 7%),
       * BG-27 line-level ALLOWANCE (line 1) AND BG-28 line-level CHARGE (line 3),
       * BG-20 document-level ALLOWANCE (19%) AND BG-21 document-level CHARGE (7%),
       * TWO BG-23 VAT breakdowns (S 19% and S 7%).
     The line/breakdown/allowance arithmetic still reconciles internally, so the
     ONLY rule the real engine fires is BR-CO-15 (fatal): the invoice total with
     VAT must equal total-without-VAT + total-VAT. Keeping BT-112 == BT-115
     leaves BR-CO-16 (payable = grand total) satisfied, so this fixture isolates
     exactly ONE distinct fatal rule with no second, unrelated violation.

     ARITHMETIC (lines/breakdowns unchanged from the good twin, EUR):
       line 1 (19%): 10 x 50.00 = 500.00 - 20.00 line allowance -> BT-131 = 480.00
       line 2 (19%):  4 x 30.00 = 120.00                         -> BT-131 = 120.00
       line 3 ( 7%):  5 x 22.00 = 110.00 + 10.00 line charge     -> BT-131 = 120.00
       line 4 ( 7%):  2 x 40.00 =  80.00                         -> BT-131 =  80.00
       BT-106 sum of line nets = 480 + 120 + 120 + 80            = 800.00
       document allowance (BG-20, 19%) BT-107 = 50.00
       document charge    (BG-21,  7%) BT-108 = 30.00
       19% breakdown base BT-116 = (480 + 120) - 50 = 550.00 -> BT-117 = 104.50
        7% breakdown base BT-116 = (120 +  80) + 30 = 230.00 -> BT-117 =  16.10
       BT-109 tax exclusive = 800 - 50 + 30 = 780.00 = 550 + 230 (sum of bases)
       BT-110 total VAT = 104.50 + 16.10 = 120.60
       DEFECT: BT-112 tax inclusive stated 990.60, must be 780.00 + 120.60 =
       900.60 -> BR-CO-15 fatal; BT-115 payable = BT-112 = 990.60 (BR-CO-16 OK) -->
